  <!-- ⚠️ STUB — PREMISES NOT YET VERIFIED. Author with /task-create, which must verify every path and
       line number below against the code. See notes/task-accuracy-audit-2026-09-18.md. -->

  <prompt>`AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeForContactAsync` awaits one `ISubjectStandingGrantReader.ReadForOrganizationAsync` per distinct active organisation, SERIALLY, and `QueryActiveOrgIdsAsync` applies no `$top` — so N is unbounded by construction. `IsRecordAccessibleAsync` and `IsOperationPermittedAsync` call `ComposeAsync` once per authorization check with no composition-level cache, so the cost multiplies per decision.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, C#/.NET, the external access evaluator.</role>
  <goal>The org-baseline read is bounded and does not scale with the number of organisations on the authorization hot path — either one batched query for N organisation ids, or an explicit bound whose truncation is VISIBLE per NFR-03 rather than silent.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">A truncated read must be visibly truncated, never silently. Reuse the `Capped` surfacing the membership walk already has rather than inventing a second shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: a batched read that partially fails must not resolve to "fewer organisations confer".</constraint>
    <constraint source="register ISS-021">Not urgent, and the reason is measurable: N is currently 0 because no organisation holds a standing grant. Do not let that make the change untested — the tests must exercise N &gt; 1.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-021. Related: tasks 042, 043, 105 (the collection-read rewrite — check for overlap before starting).</notes>
</task>
